{
  "sn4.23:0.1": "Linked Discourses 4.23 ",
  "sn4.23:0.2": "3. Māra ",
  "sn4.23:0.3": "With Godhika ",
  "sn4.23:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn4.23:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "sn4.23:1.3": "Now at that time Venerable Godhika was staying on the slopes of Isigili at the Black Rock. ",
  "sn4.23:1.4": "Then Venerable Godhika, meditating diligent, keen, and resolute, experienced temporary freedom of heart. ",
  "sn4.23:1.5": "But then he fell away from that temporary freedom of heart. ",
  "sn4.23:1.6": "For a second … ",
  "sn4.23:1.7": "",
  "sn4.23:1.8": "third … ",
  "sn4.23:1.9": "",
  "sn4.23:1.10": "fourth … ",
  "sn4.23:1.11": "",
  "sn4.23:1.12": "fifth … ",
  "sn4.23:1.13": "",
  "sn4.23:1.14": "sixth time Godhika experienced temporary freedom of heart. ",
  "sn4.23:1.15": "But for a sixth time he fell away from it. ",
  "sn4.23:1.16": "For a seventh time Godhika, meditating diligent, keen, and resolute, experienced temporary freedom of heart. ",
  "sn4.23:2.1": "Then he thought, ",
  "sn4.23:2.2": "“I’ve fallen away from this temporary freedom of heart no less than six times. ",
  "sn4.23:2.3": "Why don’t I commit suicide?” ",
  "sn4.23:2.4": "And then Māra the Wicked, knowing Godhika’s train of thought, went up to the Buddha and addressed him in verse: ",
  "sn4.23:3.1": "“O great hero, O greatly wise! ",
  "sn4.23:3.2": "Shining with power and glory. ",
  "sn4.23:3.3": "You’ve gone beyo